ub.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-beets/compare/nightly-cf0983a3-ls18...nightly-a264a76c-ls19","upstream":"Match tracks by release track ID too (#7123)\n\n## Description\n\nHybrid SACD releases on MusicBrainz list the CD layer and the SACD\nlayer(s) as separate\nmedia whose tracks share recordings; only the release track IDs differ.\n`track_distance()`\ncompares recording IDs but not release track IDs, so files from the SACD\nlayer score the\nsame against both layers. The medium-number check then puts them on\nmedium 1 (the CD\nlayer), and the import overwrites their `mb_releasetrackid` with the CD\nlayer's. Seen on\n2.14.1 with\nhttps://musicbrainz.org/release/f9b87aa8-a7cf-45e3-b760-a629ec751f62.\n\nThis compares `mb_releasetrackid` with the track's `release_track_id`,\nunder the existing\n`track_id` weight, when both are known. Items without the tag and\nnon-MusicBrainz sources\nare unaffected. Background in discussion #6614.\n\nAI disclosure: the change was drafted with an AI coding assistant. I've\nreviewed and tested\nit, and can answer questions about it.\n\n## To Do\n\n- [x] ~Documentation~ (no user-facing option changes)\n- [x] Changelog.\n- [x] Tests.","upstream_url":"https://github.com/beetbox/beets/commit/a264a76c3c0ab08c55dd0d5b41fb50606cf39014"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true","BEETSDIR=/config","EDITOR=nano"],"exposed_ports":["8337/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-a264a76c-ls19.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-a264a76c-ls19/diff.json","layers":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playgr